      "label": "The concept of 'living in the moment' as a philosophical or psychological idea",
      "description": "The phrase 'every moment' implies a mindfulness or present-moment awareness philosophy, often associated with Eastern spiritual traditions (like Buddhism) or modern self-help psychology (like mindfulness meditation). This concept is not visible in the image but is essential to understanding the depth of the message.",
